The merchandise under consideration is a Kobalt 12.5-amp heat gun, model 5208257. It features two fan speeds and a variable temperature control dial and is rated at 1500 watts. The main components are a plastic molded housing that encompasses a heating element, motor-fan assembly, power switch and power cord. It delivers hot air for heat shrinking, stripping paint, bending plastic, drying and thawing. The Kobalt 12.5-amp heat gun, model 5208257 is assembled in Thailand using components sourced from Thailand and China.

The following components are produced in Thailand: main housing, front cover and heating element. The following components are produced in China: electric motor, fan, motor support, printed circuit board assembly (PCBA), switch, power cord, wiring, knob, back cover and support ring, heat insulator and fasteners. 

Motor-fan assembly (electric motor, fan and motor support), performed in China: stamp rotor laminations from silicon steel; stack laminations and wind the rotor; build the stator; assemble the motor; press-fit the fan to the motor spindle. PCBA (SMT) (printed circuit board assembly (PCBA)), performed in China: SMT placement and reflow of the printed circuit board assembly; test the PCBA. Heating element (heating element), performed in Thailand: wind resistance wire around a core fitted with ceramic pipes; insert the core into a mica-insulated metal tube; solder the safety fuse. Housing moulding (main housing and front cover), performed in Thailand: injection-mould the housing shells and covers. Switch, cord and minor parts (switch, power cord, wiring, knob, back cover and support ring, heat insulator and fasteners), performed in China: make the switch, power cord, wiring, supports and fasteners. 

Final assembly in Thailand: press fit the fan to the motor spindle and attach the fan cover; crimp plugs to the heating element wires, add heat shrink tubing, solder wires to the switch and plug the heating element into the switch and PCBA; fasten the PCBA to the main housing, assemble the temperature knob, connect the PCBA to the motor, add the back cover and motor support; secure the power cord, add the switch slider, close the housing with screws, test, label and pack.
